From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:25:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] x86/cpufeature: use the dynamic test for _static_cpu_has()
 under tinycc

__static_cpu_has() is an asm goto whose "i" operands exist only after
inlining.  tinycc does not inline, so under __TINYC__ let
_static_cpu_has(bit) be boot_cpu_has(bit).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeature.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeature.h b/arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeature.h
index b4cc5fd1b..d2e688746 100644
--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeature.h
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeature.h
@@ -116,12 +116,20 @@ static __always_inline bool __static_cpu_has(u16 bit)
 	return false;
 }
 
+#ifdef __TINYC__
+/*
+ * tcc does not inline __static_cpu_has(), so its "i" operands cannot be
+ * immediates; use the dynamic test instead.
+ */
+#define _static_cpu_has(bit)	boot_cpu_has(bit)
+#else
 #define _static_cpu_has(bit)					\
 (								\
 	__builtin_constant_p(boot_cpu_has(bit)) ?		\
 		boot_cpu_has(bit) :				\
 		__static_cpu_has(bit)				\
 )
+#endif
 
 #define cpu_has_bug(c, bit)		cpu_has(c, (bit))
 #define set_cpu_bug(c, bit)		set_cpu_cap(c, (bit))
